course: dictionary
lesson: 4216
title: Grab: taking hold quickly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To grab is to take hold of something quickly and roughly. Read this from a news story: «A great grey owl can plunge through deep snow to grab a vole it has only heard.» The owl moves fast and seizes its food, so grab means to snatch or seize quickly.
explain: Grab also has gentler meanings. To grab a snack or grab a seat means to get something quickly, without fuss. «Up for grabs» means free for anyone to take. Look at the words around grab to tell which meaning it has.
explain: A headline is the title of a news story, and it is written to grab attention. «A headline is the title of a news story; it is short, bold and grabs attention.» Here grab means to catch your attention, so you notice it straight away.
fact: Grab is a verb: grab, grabs, grabbed, grabbing. It can also be a noun: a grab.
fact: To grab means to take hold of something quickly and roughly.
fact: To grab someone's attention means to make them notice.
fact: «Up for grabs» means free for anyone to take.
fact: «Grab hold of» means take a firm hold, as in «grab the rail if you slip».
exercise: «A great grey owl can plunge through deep snow to grab a vole it has only heard.» What does grab mean here? | To hide from something | *To take hold of something quickly | To count slowly | To sing loudly
exercise: «A headline is the title of a news story; it is short, bold and grabs attention.» What does grabs attention mean? | Makes people fall asleep | Tells the time | Costs a lot of money | *Makes people notice it
exercise: The last cake is up for grabs. What does up for grabs mean? | *Free for anyone to take | Locked in a box | Given back to the baker | Too hot to eat
test: If someone tries to grab you, what should you do? | *Yell loudly and get away | Stay very still and quiet | Ask them nicely to stop | Run into a dark room
test: «A family dog in Ohio had been gentle for years; when a toddler grabbed its tail it bit her face and she needed stitches.» What did the dog do? | It went to sleep | It ran off to fetch a ball | It wagged its tail happily | *It bit her face
exam: In «grab a bite», what does grab mean? | To count the crumbs | *To get something quickly | To put something in a box | To throw something far away
